    "text": "A coordinator configures custom instructions for a Claude Project that drafts internal procedure updates. Staff need plain language, traceable claims from approved Project references, and clear handling of missing evidence. The current instruction, 'be concise, comprehensive, and always decisive,' produces guesses and inconsistent detail. Which replacement best defines stable, consistent behaviour?",
